(ideally six or more hours a day. Leafy crops \(lettuce, spinach, herbs\) are happier with less. Spend a) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 561.50 Tm
(day or two simply watching where the sun lands and for how long. A spot that's blazing at noon may) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 545.00 Tm
(be shaded by a neighboring building by 2 p.m. - you won't know until you look.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 522.50 Tm
(Step two: pick your growing style based on what you have.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 501.00 Tm
(- No yard \(balcony, patio, windowsill, fire escape\): you're a container gardener - pots and) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 485.50 Tm
(    containers of all sizes. This is the heart of this book, and it's wonderfully flexible: you can move) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 470.00 Tm
(    pots to chase the sun, and your soil isn't at the mercy of cold ground.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 454.50 Tm
(- A small yard or shared ground space: you have the option of a small in-ground bed too - but) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 439.00 Tm
(    even then, containers are a great, low-commitment way to start.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 416.50 Tm
(Step three: start modest. The most common beginner mistake is going too big too fast. A few) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 400.00 Tm
(well-tended pots will teach you more - and feed you better - than a sprawling setup you can't keep up) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 383.50 Tm
(with. You can always add more once you've got the rhythm.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 361.00 Tm
(Don't be discouraged if your space feels small or your light imperfect. You are working with what you) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 344.50 Tm
(have, and that is exactly enough to begin.) Tj
