(The Forgotten Pots) Tj
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 244.50 Tm
(Priya almost spent her whole first budget on shiny new planters online - until her mother laughed) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 229.00 Tm
(and pointed to the balcony storage box. Inside were three plastic pots from a long-dead) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 213.50 Tm
(houseplant, a cracked bucket, and an old olive-oil tin. "Poke some holes in the bottom," her) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 198.00 Tm
(mother said, "and you have three gardens." Priya scrubbed them out, drilled drainage holes, and) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 182.50 Tm
(planted herbs the same afternoon. She spent her saved money on good organic soil and compost) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 167.00 Tm
(instead - the parts that actually mattered. Her "free" containers grew basil all summer.) Tj
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 136.50 Tm
(Your tiny farm needs three foundations: something to grow in, something to grow them in the dirt of,) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 120.00 Tm
(and something to feed that dirt. Good news - most of it is already near you.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 97.50 Tm
(1. Containers. Almost anything that holds soil and can drain will work: proper plant pots, buckets,) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 81.00 Tm
(tubs, wooden boxes, even large tins. Two rules only: it must be big enough for the plant's roots, and) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 64.50 Tm
(it must have drainage holes in the bottom so water doesn't pool and rot the roots. Look around your) Tj
