(Chapter 4: Mulch, Tools, and the No-Chemical Rule) Tj
0.720 0.470 0.100 rg
/F2 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 394.00 Tm
(The Newspaper Trick) Tj
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 378.50 Tm
(Tom couldn't understand why his pots dried out by lunchtime and sprouted weeds by the weekend) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 363.00 Tm
(- he was watering constantly and still losing the battle. An old gardener at the market told him two) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 347.50 Tm
(words: "Mulch. Newspaper." Tom laid a sheet of newspaper over the soil and topped it with a thin) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 332.00 Tm
(layer of dried leaves and twigs from the park. The change was almost unfair: his soil stayed damp) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 316.50 Tm
(for days, weeds nearly vanished, and as the mulch slowly broke down it fed the soil for free. He) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 301.00 Tm
(couldn't believe he'd been doing it the hard way all along.) Tj
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 270.50 Tm
(Two humble, nearly-free materials will make your small garden dramatically easier - and one firm) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 254.00 Tm
(rule will keep it truly organic.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 231.50 Tm
(Mulch - the hardest-working free material you'll use. Mulch is just a protective layer spread over your) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 215.00 Tm
(soil: fallen leaves, flower blossoms, twigs, pine needles, bark. It isn't only for looks. Organic mulch:) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 193.50 Tm
(- Suppresses weeds so you spend less time weeding.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 178.00 Tm
(- Holds moisture so water doesn't evaporate before your plants drink it.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 162.50 Tm
(- Steadies soil temperature - warmer in cold snaps, cooler in heat.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 147.00 Tm
(- Feeds the soil as it slowly decomposes into rich topsoil.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 124.50 Tm
(Two cautions: avoid hay \(it's full of weed seeds - you'd plant the very problem you're fighting\), and) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 108.00 Tm
(don't pile it too thick - two to three inches is plenty. Watch that it doesn't mat down \(which blocks) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 91.50 Tm
(water\) or turn slimy \(if it does, scrape it off and replace it\). A sheet of old newspaper laid under the) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 75.00 Tm
(mulch helps block weeds and deters insects.) Tj
ET
