/F2 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 503.50 Tm
(The Vegetable She Hated) Tj
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 488.00 Tm
(Lena "hated" radishes. Canned, they were mushy and bitter - a childhood nightmare. But radishes) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 472.50 Tm
(topped every "easy for beginners" list, so she reluctantly planted a few in a window box, mostly to) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 457.00 Tm
(practice. Three weeks later she pulled up a small, crisp, peppery radish, rinsed it, and took a) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 441.50 Tm
(cautious bite. She stopped mid-chew. It was nothing like the canned version - fresh, bright, almost) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 426.00 Tm
(sweet. She ate the whole handful standing at the sink. "Turns out," she laughed, "I never hated) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 410.50 Tm
(radishes. I hated the can.") Tj
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 380.00 Tm
(Choosing what to grow is the fun part - and for a beginner in a small space, the golden rule is: start) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 363.50 Tm
(with easy, fast, forgiving crops. Early success builds confidence. Don't dismiss a vegetable just) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 347.00 Tm
(because you didn't like the store version; home-grown often tastes like a different food entirely.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 324.50 Tm
(Here are beginner-friendly, small-space champions:) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 303.00 Tm
(- Tomatoes - grow in most climates; cherry types are perfect for pots and pricey in stores. Give) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 287.50 Tm
(    them sun and water; pick as soon as they ripen.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 272.00 Tm
(- Chilies & Peppers - excellent in pots, grow much of the year in good conditions, and you can) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 256.50 Tm
(    harvest them whenever you need them.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 241.00 Tm
(- Zucchini & squash - fast and dramatic \(they seem to grow overnight\); pick zucchini young and) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 225.50 Tm
(    often to keep more coming.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 210.00 Tm
(- Peas - kid-favorite, hugely productive; they need a little stake or support to climb.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 194.50 Tm
(- Radishes - one of the very first crops a beginner should try; ready fast, grow spring into fall.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 179.00 Tm
(- Lettuce - a must for salad lovers; plant before it gets too hot, thrives in cool spring.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 163.50 Tm
(- Turnips - quick and easy; both root and leaves are edible; just keep them well-watered.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 148.00 Tm
(- Carrots - need loose, deep soil \(a deep pot works\); sweet and satisfying.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 132.50 Tm
(- Green beans - pole types save space by growing up a support; great value if you buy canned) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 117.00 Tm
(    often.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 101.50 Tm
(- Spring onions - easy, need mostly water, and planted around a border they help repel pests.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 86.00 Tm
(- Beets - the roots and the tops are edible; keep them mulched.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 70.50 Tm
(- Potatoes - easy and fun \(kids love digging them up\); best in a deep container or bag.) Tj
ET
endstream
