0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 710.50 Tm
(Sam's hands shook a little on planting day - the carrot seeds were tiny as dust, and he was) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 695.00 Tm
(terrified of dumping them all in one clump. Then he remembered a trick from this very book. He) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 679.50 Tm
(rolled out a strip of toilet paper on the kitchen table, misted it with water, and laid the seeds along) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 664.00 Tm
(it one by one, perfectly spaced, using tweezers while watching TV. He folded it over, misted) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 648.50 Tm
(again, and carried his neat little "seed tape" out to the pot. No squinting outdoors, no clumps, no) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 633.00 Tm
(stress. Three weeks later his carrots came up in a tidy, evenly spaced row - and he felt like a) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 617.50 Tm
(genius.) Tj
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 587.00 Tm
(You've got your pots, soil, compost, mulch, and crops. Now - plant with a plan, don't just dig. A few) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 570.50 Tm
(minutes of thought here saves weeks of trouble later.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 548.00 Tm
(Prep the pot. Fill your container with your soil-and-compost mix. Spread a thin layer of compost) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 531.50 Tm
(through it so it's rich and ready. Make sure the soil is damp but not soggy, and don't pack it down) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 515.00 Tm
(hard - roots need air.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 492.50 Tm
(Sow smart. Follow the spacing on your seed packet - crowded plants compete and get sick. Place) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 476.00 Tm
(seeds just under the surface. If tiny seeds intimidate you, use the seed-tape trick: lay seeds on a) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 459.50 Tm
(moist strip of toilet paper at the right spacing, cover with another strip, mist, and lay the whole tape in) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 443.00 Tm
(the pot. No squinting, no clumps.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 420.50 Tm
(Or start with seedlings. You can buy seeds that have already sprouted, often in biodegradable pots) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 404.00 Tm
(you plant pot-and-all - the easiest route for nervous beginners. You can also start seeds indoors near) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 387.50 Tm
(a bright window and transplant later; biodegradable starter pots avoid transplant shock.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 365.00 Tm
(Companion planting for pest defense. Even at planting, you can build in protection: tuck onions,) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 348.50 Tm
(garlic, or herbs like basil around the edges of your pots or as a border. Their strong scents) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 332.00 Tm
(discourage many insects - free, chemical-free pest control from day one.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 309.50 Tm
(Mulch right away. Lay your newspaper, then 2-3 inches of mulch, over the soil \(mark where seeds) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 293.00 Tm
(are so you don't bury sprouts\). It holds moisture, blocks weeds, and shields against pests from the) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 276.50 Tm
(very start.) Tj
