(Chapter 9: Picking at the Perfect Moment) Tj
0.720 0.470 0.100 rg
/F2 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 355.50 Tm
(The Overnight Zucchini) Tj
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 340.00 Tm
(David checked his zucchini on Friday - small, not ready. Life got busy, and he looked again on) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 324.50 Tm
(Monday. In three days it had ballooned into a spongy, seedy club the size of his forearm, tough) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 309.00 Tm
(and flavorless. His neighbor, meanwhile, was harvesting slim, tender zucchini every couple of) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 293.50 Tm
(days and getting more fruit for it. That's when David learned the harvester's paradox: picking often) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 278.00 Tm
(doesn't empty your garden - it tells the plant to keep producing. He started checking daily. His) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 262.50 Tm
(plant rewarded him all summer.) Tj
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 232.00 Tm
(Harvest is the payoff - and timing is everything. Pick too late and vegetables turn tough, mushy, or) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 215.50 Tm
(bitter; pick at the right moment and they're at peak flavor. Around ripening time, check your pots) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 199.00 Tm
(every single day - some crops \(zucchini, beans, cucumbers\) balloon or toughen almost overnight,) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 182.50 Tm
(and many produce more the more you pick.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 160.00 Tm
(A quick harvest guide for popular small-space crops:) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 138.50 Tm
(- Tomatoes - pick as soon as they ripen; don't let them sit.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 123.00 Tm
(- Peppers & chilies - pick at any size once mature; leave longer for stronger flavor. Forgiving on) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 107.50 Tm
(    timing.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 92.00 Tm
(- Radishes - pull from marble-size up to about 1 inch; don't let them get bigger.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 76.50 Tm
(- Lettuce - harvest 50-60 days after planting, or take outer leaves earlier as "cut and come again.") Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 61.00 Tm
(- Peas - pick when pods are green, full, but still tender \(about a week after flowering\).) Tj
ET
endstream
